atching terminal artifact exist for effect_id."],"mode_specific":{"dry-run":"Repository identity, branch, remote, source HEAD, empty index, manifest paths, and worktree change hashes match the report; no Git mutation occurred.","integrate-remote-and-resume":"The integrated effect-marked commit descends from the prepared remote head, preserves the authorized manifest-only delta, equals local and remote heads, and leaves no rebase/index state.","isolated-integrate-and-resume":"The effect-marked isolated commit equals remote head, contains only the authorized manifest/overlay delta, and the source repository snapshot is byte-identical to preparation.","isolated-reconcile-and-resume":"The effect-marked reconciled commit equals remote head, contains only the authorized scope, satisfies the approved three-way/overlay/ledger rules, regenerates the blocker view canonically, and leaves the source snapshot unchanged.","publish":"The exact effect-marked local commit has the approved parent, message, metadata policy, and manifest-only delta; local HEAD and remote branch head equal that commit; the index is empty; unrelated paths retain their prepared state.","resume-push":"The authorized effect commit remains local HEAD and equals remote branch head; no new local commit was created."},"source_corrections":["Replace free repository paths and remote names with trusted repository/remote registry keys and materialized manifest sets.","Require and atomically consume an exact publication-authorization receipt for every mutating mode; contract approval alone never authorizes publication.","Add a deterministic Prevention-Effect-ID commit trailer and journaled stage receipts so a crash after commit or push can be reconciled without duplication.","Split long integration modes into progressively reserved typed stages and terminalize only after local/remote/source semantic re-observation.","Route no-argument operator use through shared semantic intake; reject operator-authored argv, derive